  "note": "Election of the whole council (12 seats at large) on 18 September 1946; 18 candidates stood and 12 were returned (Belfast News-Letter, 19 September 1946, p. 5). There were 18 candidates; the six not elected are entered without votes, which the paper does not print. The nominations (Belfast News-Letter, 6 September 1946, p. 5) name A. G. Algeo, M. Cunningham, W. M'Kee Dunlop, R. Macafee, R. M'Ilroy, D. M'Kenna, J. P. Owens, J. M. Reith, G. C. Ashe, W. Baird, H. G. Campbell, J. Donaghy, J. Fullerton, A. Getty, T. W. M'Coubrey, J. M'Cracken, T. L. M'Elderry and J. M'Naul. Losers not printed: re-checked on the British Newspaper Archive's page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 19 September 1946, p. 5 (13 Nov 2026): there were 18 candidates for 12 seats, and only the twelve elected are printed.",
  "losersNotPrinted": true,
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page images of the Belfast News-Letter, 19 September 1946, p. 5, and 6 September 1946, p. 5 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the six defeated candidates of the eighteen nominated (Cunningham, M'Ilroy, M'Kenna, Donaghy, Getty, M'Elderry) are now entered without votes; the results' misprints Reith, J. W. M'Coubrey and J. B. Owens are entered as the nominations (and the 1939 and 1958 returns) give them, J. M. Wreath, T. W. M'Coubrey and J. P. Owens, with the printed forms kept in Name_As_Printed."
